"onboarding.title" = "PinboardShot Is Running in the Menu Bar";
"onboarding.message" = "PinboardShot does not appear in the Dock. Find the viewfinder icon in the menu bar.\n\nGlobal shortcuts are disabled by default. Add only the ones you want in Settings → Shortcuts.\n\nCapturing requires Screen & System Audio Recording access. Images, annotations, and history stay on this Mac; only software updates use the network.";
"onboarding.requestPermission" = "Continue and Request Access";
"onboarding.later" = "Set Up Later";
"quickStart.title" = "PinboardShot Quick Start";
"quickStart.message" = "1. Start a region, delayed, or scrolling capture from the menu bar, or repeat the last region.\n2. Use the quick result overlay to copy, save, annotate, pin, or drag a capture into another app.\n3. The selection toolbar includes OCR, color picking, and smart redaction. Use arrow keys for precise movement and Option + arrows to resize.\n4. Create pins from the clipboard or image files. Right-click a pin to control opacity, position lock, visibility, and mouse passthrough.\n5. Search recognized text, manage results, or create a comparison board from History in Settings.\n\nGlobal shortcuts are disabled by default. Add only the ones you want in Settings.";
"letterToUsers.title" = "A Note to Users";
"letterToUsers.message" = "Thank you for using PinboardShot.\n\nI built it because everyday tools for screenshots, annotation, and pinning should feel light, quiet, and trustworthy.\n\nPinboardShot will stay free forever. It will not turn into a subscription, and core features will not be locked behind a paywall.\n\nIt does not collect, upload, or sell your data. Screenshots, annotations, history, and watermark records stay on this Mac by default. Apart from software updates, only a selected image region is sent when you explicitly configure a remote OCR plugin and actively use the OCR tool.\n\nIf something breaks, feels awkward, or would be better with a small feature, you are always welcome to open a GitHub Issue. I will read it carefully and do my best to fix it.";
